+------------------------------------------------------------
-- @DESC: recursive rule computes fibonacci (E6)
------------------------------------------------------------+
rule fib(n ∈ Z) => (r ∈ Z):
  if n < 2 do
    let r := n;
  else
    let r := fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2);
  done;
return;

rule main:
  new f6 := fib(6);
  expect f6 = 8;
  new f10 := fib(10);
  expect f10 = 55;
return;
+------------------------------------------------------------
spec/03-rules.md §5.2: a rule is bound before its body so it
may call itself (self-recursion). Unlike T0602 factorial,
fibonacci exercises two base cases and a two-way recursive
step, proving the evaluator keeps each call frame isolated.
------------------------------------------------------------+
-- @AI: No - assertion-only (self-verifying)
